<title>UK: TABLE-Standard Chartered H1 div up 24 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Standard Chartered H1 div up 24 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>				(million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		  28.8		   vs 27.3</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	   5.25		   vs 4.25</p>
<p> Pretax			 435		    vs 448</p>
<p> Trading profit	     434		    vs 402</p>
<p> Bad/doubtful debt charge  44		    vs  44</p>
<p> Net interest income	667		    vs 637</p>
<p>	 NOTE - Analysts had forecast pre-tax profits in a range</p>
<p>between 431 and 495 million stg.</p>
<p>Trading profit was up eight percent at actual exchange rates and up 16 percent at constant exchange rates.</p>
<p>Full company name - Standard Chartered Plc</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4365</p>
